$b['The American Classic'] = 'Two panels side by side on one image, divided down the middle. LEFT PANEL: the tattoo design alone on a plain white background, shown flat exactly as described, no body, drawn large so it fills most of the panel. RIGHT PANEL: Studio photograph of a real person''s body showing the same exact tattoo where described, healed tattoo on real skin in soft even light, the rest of the body modestly covered by simple plain clothing, only the tattooed area bare, plain seamless light grey studio backdrop - no room, no furniture, no scenery. The tattoo in both panels is identical. The tattoo: The American Classic - a beautifully detailed classic Harley-Davidson cruiser viewed from a low front three-quarter angle. Show the round headlamp, thick front tire, fork, sculpted fuel tank, polished chrome, and unmistakable V-twin engine. Warm highlights reflect across the metal while the background stays dark and uncluttered. A timeless American cruiser presented like a prized mechanical sculpture. Tattoo style: black-and-grey realism with selective chrome highlights. It is real tattoo art made for skin - tattoo linework, shading and colour the way a tattoo artist would ink it, not a photo or a painting pasted onto the body. The design has an open, organic shape that grows out of its own elements - no frame, no border, no oval or circle outline, no background panel behind it. The only lettering in the tattoo is the Harley-Davidson name on the motorcycle - no other text, no watermarks. In the right panel it is a tattoo on a man''s outer upper arm - it follows the shape of the body and fades softly into bare skin at its edges.'
